<div class="<%= layout_framework_classes %>">
  <div class="<%= layout_framework_title_classes %>">
    <%= render 'framework_v2/page_header', page_name: :rich_text %>
  </div>

  <div class="<%= layout_framework_content_classes %>">
    <%= render_framework_intro_paragraph(:rich_text) %>

    <div class="space-y-16">
      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Understanding Richtext Components') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            The richtext system consists of two key parts working together: the parent <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">.richtext</code> container and its natural child <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">.content</code> <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :content_limiter) %> component.
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> mt-3">
            The parent <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">.richtext</code> container is designed for flexibility and can hold any content. It controls the overall placement and spacing of the component within your layout.
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> mt-3">
            The <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">.content</code> component is where your actual text content lives. It provides additional styling and formatting options specific to text.
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> mt-3">
            Both components have separate alignment modifiers that serve different purposes. The table below summarizes each modifier:
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto mt-3">
            <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-700">
              <thead class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Class</th>
                  <th class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Modifiers</th>
                  <th class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Applies To</th>
                  <th class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Controls</th>
                  <th class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Example</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-700">
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap">
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">richtext</code>
                  </td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm">
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">left</code>,
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">center</code>,
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">right</code>
                  </td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Container (<code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">.richtext</code>)</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Aligns the richtext container within its parent</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 text-sm"><code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">richtext--center</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap">
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">content</code>
                  </td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm">
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">left</code>,
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">center</code>,
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">right</code>
                  </td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Child content (<code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">.content</code>)</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Aligns the content block within the richtext container</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 text-sm"><code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">content--right</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap">
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">text</code>
                  </td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm">
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">left</code>,
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">center</code>,
                    <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">right</code>
                  </td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Text elements inside <code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">.content</code></td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Aligns inline text within the content block</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4 text-sm"><code class="text-sm font-mono text-syntax-string">text--center</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> mt-3">
            This multi-level alignment system provides maximum flexibility for positioning both the component and its content independently.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Rich Text Alignment') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            The Rich Text component can be aligned in three different ways: left, center, or right.
            Each alignment option provides different text positioning to suit various design needs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Left Aligned') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              Left alignment is the default and most readable format for longer text content, ideal for paragraphs and articles.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout">
                      <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                        <%= image_tag "trmnl--glyph-black-large.svg", class: "image" %>
                        <div class="content content--left gap text--left">
                          <p>This is an example of left-aligned rich text content. This alignment is generally best for readability with longer paragraphs of text.</p>
                          <p>Multiple paragraphs will maintain the same alignment, making it easy to read through longer content while maintaining visual consistency.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                      <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                      <span class="instance">Left Aligned</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
  <img class="image" src="/assets/trmnl--glyph-black-large.svg">
  <div class="content content--left gap text--left">
    <p>This is an example of left-aligned rich text content.</p>
    <p>Multiple paragraphs will maintain the same alignment.</p>
  </div>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Center Aligned') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              Center alignment is ideal for headings, quotes, or shorter text that needs to be highlighted or visually balanced within the layout.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout">
                      <div class="richtext richtext--center gap--large">
                        <%= image_tag "trmnl--glyph-black-large.svg", class: "image" %>
                        <div class="content content--center gap text--center">
                          <p>This is an example of center-aligned rich text content.</p>
                          <p>Centered text works well for quotes, headings, or highlighted information that needs visual emphasis.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                      <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                      <span class="instance">Center Aligned</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="richtext richtext--center gap--large">
  <img class="image" src="/assets/trmnl--glyph-black-large.svg">
  <div class="content content--center gap text--center">
    <p>This is an example of center-aligned rich text content.</p>
    <p>Centered text works well for quotes or highlighted information.</p>
  </div>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <%= framework_heading(4, 'Right Aligned') %>
            <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
              Right alignment is less common but can be useful for specific design scenarios or to create visual tension in layouts.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout">
                      <div class="richtext richtext--right gap--large">
                        <%= image_tag "trmnl--glyph-black-large.svg", class: "image" %>
                        <div class="content content--right gap text--right">
                          <p>This is an example of right-aligned rich text content.</p>
                          <p>Right alignment can be used for captions, sidebars, or to create visual interest through contrasting alignments.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                      <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                      <span class="instance">Right Aligned</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="richtext richtext--right gap--large">
  <img class="image" src="/assets/trmnl--glyph-black-large.svg">
  <div class="content content--right gap text--right">
    <p>This is an example of right-aligned rich text content.</p>
    <p>Right alignment can be used for captions or sidebars.</p>
  </div>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Content Size Variants') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            The Rich Text component offers six size variants: <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">small</code>,
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">base</code>, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">large</code>,
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">xlarge</code>, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">xxlarge</code>,
            and <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">xxxlarge</code>.
            The <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">content</code> class without size modifiers
            and the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">content--base</code> class both produce the same visual result.
            Use <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">content--base</code> when you need to explicitly set the base size
            in responsive contexts. All size variants support responsive prefixes like <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">sm:</code>,
            <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">md:</code>, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">lg:</code>,
            and <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">portrait:</code>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout layout--col">
                      <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                        <div class="content content--xxxlarge">
                          <p>This is xxxlarge size rich text content.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="content content--xxlarge">
                          <p>This is xxlarge size rich text content.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="content content--xlarge">
                          <p>This is xlarge size rich text content.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="content content--large">
                          <p>This is large size rich text content.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="content content--base">
                          <p>This is base size rich text content.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="content content--small">
                          <p>This is small size rich text content.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                      <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                      <span class="instance">Size Variants</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <!-- XXXLarge Size -->
  <div class="content content--xxxlarge">
    <p>This is xxxlarge size rich text content.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- XXLarge Size -->
  <div class="content content--xxlarge">
    <p>This is xxlarge size rich text content.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- XLarge Size -->
  <div class="content content--xlarge">
    <p>This is xlarge size rich text content.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Large Size -->
  <div class="content content--large">
    <p>This is large size rich text content.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Base Size (same as default, useful for responsive) -->
  <div class="content content--base">
    <p>This is base size rich text content.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Small Size -->
  <div class="content content--small">
    <p>This is small size rich text content.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Responsive example -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content content--base lg:content--xxxlarge">
    <p>Base by default, xxxlarge on large screens</p>
  </div>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Controlling Width') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            By default, the Rich Text content takes up as much space as it needs and is centered in the layout, expanding up to a maximum width.
            However, you can precisely control the width of content using Size utility classes <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :size) %>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout">
                      <div class="richtext richtext--center gap--large">
                        <div class="content w--[240px] text--center gap">
                          <p>This Rich Text content has a fixed width of 240 pixels using utility classes.</p>
                          <p>Notice how the text is constrained to this specific width regardless of the container size.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                      <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                      <span class="instance">Fixed Width: 240px</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="richtext richtext--center gap--large">
  <div class="content w--[240px] text--center gap">
    <p>This Rich Text content has a fixed width of 240 pixels using utility classes.</p>
    <p>Notice how the text is constrained to this specific width regardless of the container size.</p>
  </div>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-4">
            <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
              You can use any of the Size system's fixed sizes (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">w--32</code>, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">w--64</code>, etc.),
              arbitrary sizes (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">w--[250px]</code>), or responsive sizes (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">w--full</code>, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">w--auto</code>).
              This flexibility lets you create perfectly sized text blocks for any layout need.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Responsive Features Section -->
      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Responsive Features') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            The <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">content</code> component supports all three responsive systems: size-based, orientation-based, and bit-depth variants.
            This enables precise control over content text size across different device configurations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <%= framework_heading(4, 'Breakpoint Prefixes') %>
              <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
                Use breakpoint prefixes like <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">sm:</code>,
                <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">md:</code>, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">lg:</code>
                to apply different content sizes at different screen widths.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
                <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                  <div class="screen">
                    <div class="view view--full">
                      <div class="layout layout--col items--start gap">
                        <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                          <div class="content content--base lg:content--xxlarge">
                            <p>Responsive content</p>
                          </div>
                          <div class="content content--small">
                            <p>Base by default, xxlarge on lg screens</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="title_bar">
                        <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                        <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                        <span class="instance">Responsive</span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-4">
              <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
                demo_code: '<!-- Base by default, xxlarge on lg screens -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content content--base lg:content--xxlarge">
    <p>Responsive content</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Small by default, base on medium+ screens -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content content--small md:content--base">
    <p>Small by default, base on medium+ screens</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Progressive size scaling -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content content--small sm:content--base md:content--large lg:content--xxlarge">
    <p>Progressive content sizing</p>
  </div>
</div>'
              ) %>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <%= framework_heading(4, 'Orientation and Size+Orientation') %>
              <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
                Content sizes can adapt to orientation with <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">portrait:</code> and <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">landscape:</code>, and can be combined
                with size breakpoints (e.g., <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">md:portrait:</code>).
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
                <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                  <div class="screen">
                    <div class="view view--full">
                      <div class="layout layout--col items--start gap">
                        <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                          <div class="content content--large portrait:content--small">
                            <p>Orientation variant content</p>
                          </div>
                          <div class="content content--small">
                            <p>Large by default, small in portrait.</p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="title_bar">
                        <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                        <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                        <span class="instance">Orientation</span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-4">
              <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
                demo_code: '<!-- Large by default, small in portrait -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content content--large portrait:content--small">
    <p>Orientation variant content</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Caption describing the responsive behavior -->
<div class="content content--small">Large by default, small in portrait.</div>'
              ) %>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <%= framework_heading(4, 'Bit-Depth Responsive') %>
              <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
                Use bit-depth prefixes like <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">1bit:</code>,
                <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">2bit:</code>, and
                <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">4bit:</code> to optimize content text size
                for different display color capabilities.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
                <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                  <div class="screen">
                    <div class="view view--full">
                      <div class="layout layout--col gap--large">
                        <div class="flex flex--col gap--medium flex--center">
                          <div class="flex flex--col flex--center">
                            <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                              <div class="content 1bit:content--large 2bit:content--xlarge 4bit:content--xxlarge">
                                <p>Display optimized content</p>
                              </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="content content--small">
                              <p>Large (1bit) → XLarge (2bit) → XXLarge (4bit)</p>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                          <div class="w--full border--h-6"></div>
                          <div class="flex flex--col flex--center">
                            <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                              <div class="content 1bit:content--base 4bit:content--xlarge">
                                <p>Selective sizing</p>
                              </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="content content--small">
                              <p>Base (1bit) → XLarge (4bit)</p>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="title_bar">
                        <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                        <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                        <span class="instance">Bit-Depth Responsive</span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-4">
              <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
                demo_code: '<!-- Different content sizes for different bit-depth displays -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content 1bit:content--large 2bit:content--xlarge 4bit:content--xxlarge">
    <p>Display optimized content</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Selective bit-depth targeting -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content 1bit:content--base 4bit:content--xlarge">
    <p>Selective sizing</p>
  </div>
</div>'
              ) %>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <%= framework_heading(4, 'Combined Responsive Features') %>
              <p class="<%= framework_subsection_description_classes %>">
                Combine multiple responsive systems for highly targeted content sizing. Use size, orientation,
                and bit-depth modifiers together following the pattern:
                <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">size:orientation:bit-depth:content--size</code>.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
                <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                  <div class="screen">
                    <div class="view view--full">
                      <div class="layout layout--col gap--large">
                        <div class="flex flex--col gap--medium flex--center">
                          <div class="flex flex--col flex--center">
                            <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                              <div class="content md:portrait:2bit:content--xlarge lg:4bit:content--xxlarge">
                                <p>Advanced targeting</p>
                              </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="content content--small">
                              <p>Complex responsive combinations</p>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                          <div class="w--full border--h-6"></div>
                          <div class="flex flex--col flex--center">
                            <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                              <div class="content sm:1bit:content--large md:portrait:content--base lg:4bit:content--xlarge">
                                <p>Multi-condition content</p>
                              </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="content content--small">
                              <p>Multiple responsive conditions</p>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="title_bar">
                        <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                        <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                        <span class="instance">Combined Responsive</span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-4">
              <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
                demo_code: '<!-- Highly targeted responsive combinations -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content md:portrait:2bit:content--xlarge lg:4bit:content--xxlarge">
    <p>Advanced targeting</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Multiple responsive conditions -->
<div class="richtext gap--large">
  <div class="content sm:1bit:content--large md:portrait:content--base lg:4bit:content--xlarge">
    <p>Multi-condition content</p>
  </div>
</div>'
              ) %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Integration with Content Limiter') %>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            The Rich Text component works seamlessly with the Content Limiter utility <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :content_limiter) %> to handle overflowing text. When combined,
            it automatically adjusts text size to fit the available space, which is particularly useful in constrained layouts.
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> mt-3">
            Simply add the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-content-limiter="true"</code> attribute to your richtext content element. You can also specify a custom maximum height using the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-content-max-height</code> attribute (e.g., <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-content-max-height="140"</code>).
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> mt-3">
            When <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-content-limiter="true"</code> is present, the limiter auto-measures the available height in the nearest container and adjusts text to fit. You can override the auto height by specifying <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-content-max-height</code> with a pixel value.
          </p>

          <div class="<%= message_sage_classes %> mt-4">
            <div class="flex items-center w-full">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 items-center">
                <%= render 'shared/icons/info' %>
              </div>
              <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between ml-3">
                <p class="leading-none text-sm font-medium">
                  Automatically resize text when content exceeds height limits
                </p>
                <p class="text-sm md:mt-0 md:ml-6">
                  <%= link_to framework_docs_content_limiter_path, class: "#{button_small_classes} #{button_sage_solid_classes}", target: :_blank do %>
                    View Content Limiter Documentation
                    <%= render 'shared/icons/arrow_right' %>
                  <% end %>
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <div class="mashup mashup--2x2">
                    <div class="view view--quadrant">
                      <div class="layout">
                        <div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
                          <div class="content" data-content-limiter="true">
                            <p class="text--left">
                              The Rich Text component with Content Limiter will automatically adjust text size when content exceeds the auto-measured available height. This is particularly useful for views with limited vertical space such as quadrants or half-horizontal layouts.
                              <br><br>
                              Notice how this text is rendered smaller to fit within the quadrant view. Without Content Limiter, this text would overflow the container.
                            </p>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </div>

                      <div class="title_bar">
                        <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                        <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                        <span class="instance">With Content Limiter</span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="richtext richtext--left gap--large">
  <div class="content" data-content-limiter="true">
    <p class="text--left">
      The Rich Text component with Content Limiter will automatically
      adjust text size when content exceeds the height threshold.
      This is particularly useful for views with limited vertical space.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Integration with Pixel Perfect') %>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            For optimal text rendering on ePaper displays, the Rich Text component can be enhanced with the Pixel Perfect utility <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :pixel_perfect) %>.
            This ensures text is rendered with crisp edges by aligning precisely to the pixel grid, preventing blurry or inconsistent text weight.
          </p>

          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %> mt-3">
            Simply add the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">data-pixel-perfect="true"</code> attribute to your richtext content element.
          </p>

          <div class="<%= message_sage_classes %> mt-4">
            <div class="flex items-center w-full">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 items-center">
                <%= render 'shared/icons/info' %>
              </div>
              <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-between ml-3">
                <p class="leading-none text-sm font-medium">
                  Ensure crisp text rendering on 1-bit displays
                </p>
                <p class="text-sm md:mt-0 md:ml-6">
                  <%= link_to framework_docs_pixel_perfect_path, class: "#{button_small_classes} #{button_sage_solid_classes}", target: :_blank do %>
                    View Pixel Perfect Documentation
                    <%= render 'shared/icons/arrow_right' %>
                  <% end %>
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="<%= framework_example_classes %>">
            <div class="<%= framework_example_inner_classes %>">
              <div class="<%= framework_example_wrapper_classes %>">
                <div class="screen">
                  <div class="view view--full">
                    <div class="layout">
                      <div class="richtext gap">
                        <div class="content content--center text--center" data-pixel-perfect="true"><p>This text is rendered with pixel perfect alignment, ensuring that each character aligns precisely with the pixel grid. Notice how the text appears crisp and clear with consistent weight.</p></div>
                        <div class="content content--center text--center" data-pixel-perfect="true"><p>Pixel Perfect is especially important for ePaper displays that use a 1-bit color space (just black and white), where anti-aliased gray pixels are forced to become either fully black or fully white.</p></div>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="title_bar">
                      <%= image_tag plugin_image_path("trmnl--render.svg"), class: "image", alt: "TRMNL Logo" %>
                      <span class="title">Rich Text</span>
                      <span class="instance">With Pixel Perfect</span>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <%= render CodeExampleComponent.new(
              demo_code: '<div class="richtext richtext--left gap">
  <div class="content" data-pixel-perfect="true">
    <p>
      This text is rendered with pixel perfect alignment, ensuring that each character aligns precisely with the pixel grid. Notice how the text appears crisp and clear with consistent weight.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="content" data-pixel-perfect="true">
    <p>
      Pixel Perfect is especially important for ePaper displays that use a 1-bit color space (just black and white), where anti-aliased gray pixels are forced to become either fully black or fully white.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>'
            ) %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <%= render 'framework_v2/page_navigation' %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
